{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T22:25:36.294228Z","id":"a5f60f0ec06a9f866fe4d0fd87c15b5a2bb0a37604e1ad009f6c2f42dc3a3687","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"827df625c91cfc9e6bd45747f9298c80317d4ca3ae53a9d40fdd6fdce6f1aa1c","summary":"Fixed in git:a9ecb07d1: affordable() prices the uncached tail at the cache-write rate, the cached prefix at cached_input, output at output. Test pricing::the_input_bound_is_priced_at_the_cache_write_rate (a dear cache-write rate stops the run credits_exhausted; the same input rate does not) passes; bazel test //crates/clax-bot/... passed (lib and integration: 'test result: ok. 59 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored'); SHAs are unsigned and change on re-signing. Proposed close.","tags":["session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T22:25:36.294530Z","id":"55067ea9d3ec7aaf9c91f9275c2a209b803e5e1e97aceafe32053251bd719fc4","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"16e5088f83fd02c99e03041e121b8aa3d37cb7e039648ce126c5ba45563d44dd","summary":"Fixed in git:a9ecb07d1: the turn keeps the rates its answering attempt snapshotted (call_rates) and charges the committed rows at them. money::a_repeated_call_is_priced_as_it_was_made and pricing::a_billed_cost_survives_a_resumed_run pass; bazel test //crates/clax-bot/... passed (lib and integration: 'test result: ok. 59 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored'); SHAs are unsigned and change on re-signing. Proposed close.","tags":["session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T22:25:36.294830Z","id":"913e6eb6078bd21d3f569765476e66c728ea9c074bf0b6ca3619a93cfaf6ad34","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"e4c812158e771dbcfbd239be55e8034e311f463e80443ae7b713344b082b587e","summary":"Fixed in git:a9ecb07d1: priced() resolves a billed row without a snapshotted rate (line_token_rate -> token_rate) before bill(), and Tick::rates returns the store's error instead of dropping the unit. Test run::tests::a_billed_row_without_a_snapshotted_rate_is_resolved_before_billing passes; bazel test //crates/clax-bot/... passed (lib and integration: 'test result: ok. 59 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored'); SHAs are unsigned and change on re-signing. Proposed close.","tags":["session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T22:25:36.295129Z","id":"5401556c70b48bd120b7c8ebbd5d00c3cfec29fbcfff185272e0efc89a3a892a","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"87e8296d8c6e5e6657e3d05933954369313255f0d264b7a12a84741629fb9c3b","summary":"Fixed in git:a9ecb07d1: run::tests::a_mixed_card_bills_the_cost_based_rows_and_keeps_the_credit_based_ones, a_row_over_a_million_tokens_falls_short_by_under_its_millions, a_billed_cost_of_0_charges_no_credits_on_cost_based_rows and a_billed_row_without_a_snapshotted_rate_is_resolved_before_billing pass; bazel test //crates/clax-bot/... passed (lib and integration: 'test result: ok. 59 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored'); SHAs are unsigned and change on re-signing. Proposed close.","tags":["session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T22:28:28.476926Z","id":"6f80a64bd422620dbb688667209235a5f684d167abf6c61c497f3ba1c333ede8","body":{"detail":"The cache-write rate is right for the Messages API, where with_breakpoint (run.rs:695-708) puts cache_control on the last block. The Chat Completions and Gemini translators send no cache_control (crates/clax-sample/src/messages/openai.rs, gemini.rs). gemini.rs:396 always reports cache_creation_input_tokens 0. openai.rs:450-455 reports it only from prompt_tokens_details.cache_write_tokens. So on those APIs the uncached tail is billed at the input rate. At the default rates (cache_write 700 000 vs input 560 000 milli-credits a million) the bound reserves 25 % more of the input than will be charged: max_tokens is cut, and a run near its credits is stopped credits_exhausted although it could still afford a turn. A rate card whose cache_write is below input (an admin setting it to 0 for an API that never writes cache) makes the bound too low the other way, and max_tokens can overshoot the credits left. A catalog listing without a cache-write price falls back to the input cost, so catalog rates are unaffected. pricing::the_input_bound_is_priced_at_the_cache_write_rate covers only the default (anthropic) api.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1762},"end":{"line":1769},"content_hash":"b361da1e33be0209bd57cb2b62df59d02af554201fa8cd987a488358449251e7"},"suggested_fix":"Price the tail at the cache-write rate only when settings.api is the Messages API (ModelApi::Anthropic), and at the input rate otherwise; or take the larger of the two credit amounts per token. Add a case with settings.api openai.","summary":"affordable() prices the uncached input at the cache-write rate on every API, but on the openai and gemini APIs it is billed as input","tags":["pricing","credits","providers","review","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T22:28:28.477037Z","id":"1b312b12dab558d0ee46c32ade8694f39ffe1cb3c6d882223197905cc5da7995","body":{"detail":"Line 1712 holds only 'an own key is waived' and the clause continues on 1713; rustfmt does not reflow comments.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1710},"end":{"line":1715},"content_hash":"4dc4327efc70815eeb7a928840781d3e5ab54749e48a367409f408d23980ee76"},"suggested_fix":"Reflow the paragraph to the surrounding width.","summary":"affordable()'s doc comment breaks mid-sentence after 'a unit an own key is waived'","tags":["style","review","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T22:28:28.477685Z","id":"d81e1a72c88f4551d253f1d7e5d32fddbb43582bf843e8b0bbe7f586ed2c9d96","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"a223ade985b18f024a68b41e5ffdf081c375f976ef8939e79cde64d55b91ef3a","summary":"This re-anchor follows the drifted line numbers, not the code. 94a4332d was recorded on History::of (run.rs:556-564 at 20c92cf00), but the new span 563:572 is usage_of; History::of now starts at run.rs:575. Re-anchor it there, with a span covering History::of.","tags":["session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T22:28:28.478052Z","id":"0a1a3a820607198cafc40995734d6c594221b89b0d205f33228cbfef97ce94e4","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"512cb24a0272168d831772fd11480f5c977e3120110dd14ad03ff4a19ff89b26","summary":"Not verbatim: the re-anchors of 96939966, 94a4332d, 6f3e5c2c and 2f8fe438 change their session tag from session:claude-code:7580ce1b-... (the session that wrote them) to this branch's session, so the record no longer names the session it came from. This record's detail also keeps 'the rest at the input rate' and then appends that a9ecb07d1 changed it to the cache-write rate. Keep the original tags, and either keep the detail exactly or restate it with the current behaviour.","tags":["session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T22:30:19.263355Z","id":"d5508d796427ba5e37c93c32f1e686b7f316a843b1af9c392e80837b013a5b78","body":{"detail":"tick reads run_with_steps and History::of parses each payload (assistant blocks, script code and outcome, the first turn's system prompt) to rebuild the messages, so a run of N steps does O(N) work and reads O(total payload) per tick, O(N^2) over the run. Bounded by max_steps (40 by default); a cache of the history keyed by the last committed step would make it O(1).\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from its original record by mailto:alex@kesling.co (94a4332d), after crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs moved.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":575},"end":{"line":636},"content_hash":"8e8e29c05e8e590bdae85e7966b0796756cd3f0ef6d45a96e7331f6b3d060f26"},"summary":"Every tick rebuilds the whole history from every committed step's payload","supersedes":"a223ade985b18f024a68b41e5ffdf081c375f976ef8939e79cde64d55b91ef3a","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T22:30:19.437235Z","id":"f2d3a8fb88941108f791d9f42d9e195cabb60ee5b05cf20e17c0c7d9725dd522","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"6f80a64bd422620dbb688667209235a5f684d167abf6c61c497f3ba1c333ede8","summary":"Fixed: affordable() prices the uncached input at cache_write only when settings.api is ModelApi::Anthropic, at the input rate on openai and gemini. Test pricing::off_the_messages_api_the_input_bound_is_priced_at_the_input_rate (both APIs: a dear cache-write rate does not bound the turn, a dear input rate stops it credits_exhausted) passes. Commit 76e4dc506 (unsigned; SHA changes on re-signing); bazel test //crates/clax-bot/... passed (integration 'test result: ok. 60 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored', lib '25 passed'). Proposed close.","tags":["session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
