{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-02T00:37:08.132284Z","id":"d0a80285b0b3fcb2450558fea43c995c6bf9e0627b0580709fd093db3c92a1b8","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:caee7184224e","summary":"Fixed in git:caee71842 (with 7abc1ef16). Evidence, from the reply on this thread: Follow-up to the 7abc1ef16 fix: the cache-write tail now applies on the Messages API alone (record 6f80a64b). pricing::the_input_bound_is_priced_at_the_cache_write_rate and pricing::off_the_messages_api_the_input_bound_is_priced_at_the_input_rate pass. Commit caee71842; bazel test //crates/clax-bot/... passed (integration 'test result: ok. 60 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored', lib '25 passed'). Proposed close.","supersedes":"827df625c91cfc9e6bd45747f9298c80317d4ca3ae53a9d40fdd6fdce6f1aa1c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-02T00:37:08.225260Z","id":"02cd038648139c93618dd8830bb63c3a2133ad4547fb06e63db6346adaff950f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:caee7184224e","summary":"Fixed in git:caee71842. Evidence, from the reply on this thread: Fixed: affordable()'s doc comment is reflowed and states the per-API input pricing. Commit caee71842; bazel test //crates/clax-bot/... passed (integration 'test result: ok. 60 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored', lib '25 passed'). Proposed close.","supersedes":"1b312b12dab558d0ee46c32ade8694f39ffe1cb3c6d882223197905cc5da7995","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-02T00:37:08.317617Z","id":"8d00faf5d82ddc13bfd4c030f277e204e0a160f64b0b4a91aa3fc8b41933857f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:caee7184224e","summary":"Fixed in git:caee71842. Evidence, from the reply on this thread: Fixed: affordable() prices the uncached input at cache_write only when settings.api is ModelApi::Anthropic, at the input rate on openai and gemini. Test pricing::off_the_messages_api_the_input_bound_is_priced_at_the_input_rate (both APIs: a dear cache-write rate does not bound the turn, a dear input rate stops it credits_exhausted) passes. Commit caee71842; bazel test //crates/clax-bot/... passed (integration 'test result: ok. 60 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored', lib '25 passed'). Proposed close.","supersedes":"6f80a64bd422620dbb688667209235a5f684d167abf6c61c497f3ba1c333ede8","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-02T00:37:08.412918Z","id":"01b073b21daf1c35c733bc184227951a0884a6b9a7854e06b4af657afce95904","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7abc1ef162f1","summary":"Fixed in git:7abc1ef16. Evidence, from the reply on this thread: Fixed in git:7abc1ef16: the turn keeps the rates its answering attempt snapshotted (call_rates) and charges the committed rows at them. money::a_repeated_call_is_priced_as_it_was_made and pricing::a_billed_cost_survives_a_resumed_run pass; bazel test //crates/clax-bot/... passed (lib and integration: 'test result: ok. 59 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored'); SHAs are unsigned and change on re-signing. Proposed close.","supersedes":"16e5088f83fd02c99e03041e121b8aa3d37cb7e039648ce126c5ba45563d44dd","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-02T00:37:08.508048Z","id":"58dc052aa688b685650f230514d7e646d6bbbc553c96f1c78f26a1746c712248","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7abc1ef162f1","summary":"Fixed in git:7abc1ef16. Evidence, from the reply on this thread: Fixed in git:7abc1ef16: run::tests::a_mixed_card_bills_the_cost_based_rows_and_keeps_the_credit_based_ones, a_row_over_a_million_tokens_falls_short_by_under_its_millions, a_billed_cost_of_0_charges_no_credits_on_cost_based_rows and a_billed_row_without_a_snapshotted_rate_is_resolved_before_billing pass; bazel test //crates/clax-bot/... passed (lib and integration: 'test result: ok. 59 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored'); SHAs are unsigned and change on re-signing. Proposed close.","supersedes":"87e8296d8c6e5e6657e3d05933954369313255f0d264b7a12a84741629fb9c3b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T05:19:13.364654Z","id":"fea59b4e1e486287218d23962cc8d6b7ad830e0ddb1d8f7080b53bea600268dd","body":{"detail":"The Performer::Web arm answers web_disabled (uncharged, journaled like a policy refusal) whatever the run's WebShape (crates/clax-bot/src/web/access.rs) declares, so a run whose prompt declares clax.web.search or clax.web.fetch (crates/clax-bot/src/api.rs dts) is told it may call them and is refused at each call. Nothing declares them yet in production: Bot::web_configured is false on both hosts (crates/clax-http/src/bot.rs, crates/clax-server/src/bot.rs, crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs), so start_run (crates/clax-server/src/routes/bot.rs) writes web \"\" on every run. The arm is to be replaced by the checks of spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-02-claxbot-web-tools-design.md §4.2 and §6.3 (declared, enabled now, cap, URL rule and sources, page store, credits, source call, Spend transaction) before any host sets web_configured.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":341},"end":{"line":351},"content_hash":"4997f45140a6505b678c91a181384005fa67eccc345ba222f7b948efd626430b"},"summary":"Every clax.web.* call is refused web_disabled: RunHost::perform has no web source to call yet","tags":["session:claude-code:ad4c0f0d-1745-4445-8c27-3925ac4b061a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/api.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T05:19:13.364744Z","id":"95102b6355d5b44fab68c0004ac7b4e695a99626bbbfcb5314918fe4fd1781f9","body":{"detail":"Spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-02-claxbot-web-tools-design.md §6.1 declares `format?: \"auto\" | \"raw\"`. api::Ty has no string-literal type, so the declaration (crates/clax-bot/src/api.web.d.ts.golden) says `format?: string` and the op's doc names the two values; check_args accepts any string, so the performer must refuse any other value invalid_args. A Ty::Lit (TypeScript literal, JSON Schema const, checked by check_args) would put the two values in the declaration and the argument check.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":556},"end":{"line":563},"content_hash":"3a84c23cc3d1c0ab39858c3dcd8496912f01d989aa63b3da1d135d867591607a"},"summary":"web.fetch's opts.format is declared `string`, not the spec's `\"auto\" | \"raw\"`","tags":["revisit:a script passes a format other than auto or raw, or a second operation takes an enumerated string","session:claude-code:ad4c0f0d-1745-4445-8c27-3925ac4b061a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/api.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T05:27:39.405901Z","id":"0112a7caeddde42e39c2aa4d3ddba9e45ae91012f9164d9cf3335474e42440f4","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:680a2c05c","summary":"Taken: api::Ty::Enum declares web.fetch's opts.format as \"auto\" | \"raw\" (crates/clax-bot/src/api.web.d.ts.golden), its JSON Schema as a string enum, and check_args refuses another value invalid_args. Evidence: bazel test //crates/clax-bot:clax_bot_lib_test passes api::tests::the_sandbox_knows_every_op_whatever_the_shape (format \"html\" -> 'argument 2 (opts).format must be one of auto, raw') and dts_with_web_matches_its_golden.","supersedes":"95102b6355d5b44fab68c0004ac7b4e695a99626bbbfcb5314918fe4fd1781f9","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:ad4c0f0d-1745-4445-8c27-3925ac4b061a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T05:45:47.404481Z","id":"b4d21d32af9823099ac6db0c7c88cc061b7c249f3689d0f07ff5eb45f829e80f","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"fea59b4e1e486287218d23962cc8d6b7ad830e0ddb1d8f7080b53bea600268dd","summary":"Replaced in git:53a0db82a: the Performer::Web arm of RunHost::perform now calls RunHost::web (crates/clax-bot/src/script/web.rs), which performs web.search and web.fetch through Deps::web with the shape, grant, URL rule, page store, cap, credit and Spend checks; a run whose Deps::web is None still answers web_disabled. Evidence: bazel test //crates/clax-bot:integration passes, including web::a_search_then_a_fetch_of_a_result_is_answered_and_charged_twice and web::a_host_without_a_source_refuses_web_disabled. Proposed close: fixed in git:53a0db82a.","tags":["session:claude-code:ad4c0f0d-1745-4445-8c27-3925ac4b061a"]}}
